  "methodology": [
    "Fresh node, same artifact/binaries as live.json; 35 gameplay calls followed by 15 status-only calls to the same Doom contract",
    "Client spans from perf_counter_ns; block open/close and indexer timestamps from existing hogd INFO logs, with millisecond resolution",
    "Receipt polling gaps overlap node work; their sum is not removable delay",
    "Block open-to-close includes preparation, executor/syscalls, and proposal bookkeeping; individual internal spans are not yet instrumented",
    "Status-only call skips Doom simulation and snapshot restoration but still loads the large contract and runs a real transaction",
    "Preparation microbenchmark uses the same pinned production VM sources, compiled by Zig with -O3; separate process/toolchain from the node, so it is not an exact attribution of the node total",
    "Medians of separate spans do not add exactly; tracing and host variance may change totals versus the prior 52.31 ms run"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "The prepared contract cache is cleared at block reset; one transaction per block repeats artifact loading and translation",
    "Program preparation is outside the standalone runner tick timer",
    "Most wall time is inside the node; chain tip, signing and submission together cost about 1.5 ms"
  ],
